   "evidence": "Lines 196\u2013202; `Complex.I_sq : I ^ 2 = -1` at mathlib/Mathlib/Basic/Complex/Basic.lean:626. `real_inner_comm` (mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/Basic.lean:61) only exchanges `\u27eax,y\u27eb` for `\u27eay,x\u27eb`, which after `PiLp.inner_apply`/`conj_trivial` differs solely by factor order within each summand \u2014 something `ring`/`linear_combination` absorbs.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Lattice/Continuation/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Replace the `ring_nf; rw [I_sq]; ring` tail with `linear_combination (x (Sum.inl 0) : \u2102) * (y (Sum.inl 0) : \u2102) * Complex.I_sq` (coefficient adjusted to the actual orientation), which feeds `I ^ 2 = -1` to the ring normalizer instead of rewriting its output; then drop `rw [\u2190 real_inner_comm]`, or add a comment if it is still needed.",
   "issue": "`ring_nf; rw [I_sq]; ring` in `complexMinkowskiProduct_continuation`: the `rw` only fires if `ring_nf` happens to leave a literal `I ^ 2` atom, so a change in `ring_nf`'s normal form (e.g. `I * I`, or a different factor grouping) silently breaks the proof. The preceding `rw [\u2190 real_inner_comm]` is likewise unexplained.",
   "line": 200
  }
